  "facts": [
    "Opened in 1927, the Holland Tunnel was the world's first mechanically ventilated underwater tunnel, showcasing innovative engineering by chief engineer Clifford Milburn Holland and his successor Ole Singstad.",
    "With a diameter of 29.5 feet, each tube of the Holland Tunnel is designed to accommodate two lanes of traffic, providing a vertical clearance of 12 feet 6 inches.",
    "The Holland Tunnel's ventilation system includes 84 fans, capable of moving vast amounts of air, ensuring safety and comfort for the millions of vehicles that pass through each year."
